{{ 'crooks-bag-drawer.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  The bag drawer shell.

  Rendered once from theme.liquid, on every template, so the bag opens in place
  wherever the shopper is instead of costing them a page load and their scroll
  position.

  Empty on arrival: the contents are fetched from {{ routes.cart_url }}?view=crk-drawer
  the first time it opens, so a page that is never used to open the bag pays
  nothing for it beyond this markup.

  Progressive enhancement. The bag link in the header is a real link to /cart
  and stays one — crooks-bag-drawer.js intercepts the click only once it has
  loaded. With JS off, or if this file fails, the cart page is still there and
  still works. The full bag is also linked from inside the drawer, deliberately:
  a drawer is a shortcut, not a replacement for the page that can do everything.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="crk-root crk-bagdrawer" data-crk-bagdrawer hidden>
  <div class="crk-bagdrawer__scrim" data-crk-bag-close tabindex="-1"></div>

  <aside
    class="crk-bagdrawer__panel"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="crk-bagdrawer-title"
    data-crk-bagdrawer-panel
  >
    <header class="crk-bagdrawer__head">
      <h2 class="crk-bagdrawer__title" id="crk-bagdrawer-title">
        {{ settings.crk_bag_title | default: 'THE BAG' }}
        <span class="crk-bagdrawer__count" data-crk-bag-headcount></span>
      </h2>
      <button type="button" class="crk-bagdrawer__close" data-crk-bag-close>
        <span aria-hidden="true">&#10005;</span>
        <span class="crk-sr">{{ settings.crk_bag_close | default: 'Close the bag' }}</span>
      </button>
    </header>

    <div class="crk-bagdrawer__body" data-crk-bag-body aria-busy="false">
      <p class="crk-bagdrawer__loading" data-crk-bag-loading>{{ settings.crk_bag_loading | default: 'OPENING THE BAG&hellip;' }}</p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'crooks-bag-drawer.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
